 This document covers some of the more advanced features of Requests.
 
+Case-Insensitive Dictionary
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+``CaseInsensitiveDict`` supports mapping union operations:
+
+* ``a | b`` and ``dict | a`` return a new ``CaseInsensitiveDict``.
+* ``a |= b`` updates ``a`` in place and preserves its identity.
+
+The operands must be mappings. When keys differ only by case, the
+right-hand value and spelling win. Existing key order is preserved, and
+new keys are appended in right-hand order.
+
 Session Objects
 ---------------
 
 The Session object allows you to persist certain parameters across requests. It also persists cookies across all requests made from the Session instance, and will use ``urllib3``'s connection pooling. So if you’re making several requests to the same server, the underlying TCP connection will be reused, which can result in a significant performance increase (see HTTP persistent connection).
 
